# UNLOCK — Architecture

UNLOCK is a modular monolith with practical Clean Architecture/DDD-like boundaries.

Preferred dependency direction:
`Presentation/Routes → Application → Domain`, with infrastructure implementing ports.

Guardrails:
- domain logic does not depend on Next.js/UI;
- application orchestrates use cases, not HTTP details;
- infrastructure owns PostgreSQL/provider details;
- routes stay thin;
- Learning Engine rules do not live in React components/routes/SQL accidentally;
- reuse existing module boundaries before creating new architecture;
- avoid premature microservices/distributed infrastructure.

Canonical architecture: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` + relevant ADRs.
